## DockerHDDM model codes
C:.
├───aDDM_Garcia_LE_ES_EE.py                    # plots the specified model/s for Study 1
├───aDDM_Garcia_run_all_mod.py                 # runs the specified model/s for Study 2
├───aDDM_OV_LE_ES_EE.py                        # plots the specified model/s for Study 2
├───aDDM_OV_run_all_mod.py                     # runs the specified model/s for Study 2
├───DIC_ranking.py                             # ranks DIC files 
├───run_hddm.sh                                # runs the specified python code on the cluster
├───data_sets                                  # Folder containing the main datasets. Items with the prefix "garcia" or "Garcia" belong to Study 1, whereas items prefixed with "OV" belong to Study 2
│   ├───data_sets_Garcia                       # Study 1
│   └───data_sets_OV                           # Study 2
├───figures_dir_garcia                         # folders containing the figures for Study 1
│   └───macleod_cluster_out                  
│       ├───garcia_replication_EE_0            # EE phase, basic addm model
│       │   └───diagnostics                    # diagnostics files always contain useful diagnostic files, e.g. DIC, Rhat, images, etc....
│       ├───garcia_replication_For_paper_1
│       │   └───diagnostics
│       └───garcia_replication_LE_RL_1
│           └───diagnostics
├───figures_dir_OV                                      # folder with figures and diagnostics for Study 2
│   └───macleod_cluster_out
│       ├───OV_replication_For_paper_1
│       │   └───diagnostics
│       └───OV_replication_LE_RL_1
│           └───diagnostics
├───models_dir_garcia                               # the actual models, however, are on the cluster
├───models_dir_OV                                   # the actual models, however, are on the cluster
└───param_recovery_and_correlations
    └───correlations.py                             # Correlations - learning rate and ESaDDM+z+a~OV
    └───param_rec_individual.py                     # Parameter recovery for group and participant level
    └───param_rec_individuals_plotting.py           # participant level plotting for parameter recovery
    └───simulation_ppc.py                           # hddm built-in ppc, but not useed
    └───sp_phase_conf_stated_prob_corr.py           # confidence 
    └───sp_RMSE.py                                  # Correlations between the best aDDM & RMSE in the SP phase


# Steps involved in getting the images running on the cluster (HDDM & MNE)


# go to https://remote.abdn.ac.uk/vdesk/webtop.eui?webtop=/Common/remote.abnd.ac.uk_Azure_SP_Access_Profile-RemoteAccess_SSL_Webtop_Full&webtop_type=webtop_full (or your uni's remote access)
# and log into macleod1 (or your university's remote login)
# you need to log in with your uni account (email) and password
# once on the cluster, cd into sharedscratch which is the location you can keep all your files and output and folders and so on
# but cd outside of sharedscratch for now, there you need set up a containers folder which holds your images, see below for code:

# Load Singularity
~cd containers
module load singularity

# Pull the prebuilt HDDM image
singularity pull hddm_latest.sif docker://hcp4715/hddm:latest

